#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0009 expect=skipped domain=AE
#note "SILENCE-CHANNEL CONTRAST (executed-but-silent, not skipped). Every criterion column is present and set to N, and the AESER column is absent. The rule EXECUTES because PMDA-SD0009 declares NO Requirements.Variables -- nothing gates it -- and reports nothing because the machine-emitted var_exists(\"AESER\") conjunct at the head of the shipped expression folds FALSE. Contrast: the byte-identical situation on PMDA-SD1449 / PMDA-SD1064 / PMDA-SD1068 is expect=skipped, because those rules declared Requirements.Variables.All first; since the phase-4 hoist SD0009 declares one too. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the rule now declares the gate variable in Requirements.Variables.All, so the absent column takes the auditable SKIP this scenario pins (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AESCAN  type=Char label="Involves Cancer"
col AESCONG type=Char label="Congenital Anomaly or Birth Defect"
col AESDISAB type=Char label="Persist or Signif Disability/Incapacity"
col AESDTH  type=Char label="Results in Death"
col AESHOSP type=Char label="Requires or Prolongs Hospitalization"
col AESLIFE type=Char label="Is Life Threatening"
col AESMIE  type=Char label="Other Medically Important Serious Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE | N | N | N | N | N | N | N
S1 | AE | 001 | 2 | NAUSEA   | N | N | N | N | N | N | N
